# Two small entries for internal/termout's reader test, compiled with
#   tic -x -o testdata/term/terminfo testdata/term/terminfo/imux-test.src
# (Homebrew's tic writes the 32-bit format for imux-test-wide, whose colors do not fit in 16 bits).
imux-test|terminal for the reader test,
	am, xenl,
	cols#80, lines#24, colors#256,
	clear=\E[H\E[2J, cup=\E[%i%p1%d;%p2%dH, smcup=\E[?1049h$<5>, el=\E[K,
	AX, XT, Ext@,
	Smulx=\E[4\:%p1%dm, Ss=\E[%p1%d q, Sync=\E[?2026%?%p1%{1}%-%tl%eh%;,
	Num#7,
imux-test-wide|terminal for the reader test with 32-bit numbers,
	colors#16777216, pairs#65536, use=imux-test,
# The other entries here are copied from ncurses 6.6.20251230's compiled database, for
# cmd/termfixture's recordings. They are in first-letter directories: Debian's and Ubuntu's
# ncurses do not look in the hexadecimal ones macOS's uses.
